DESCRIPTION:Join us for an interactive\, movement-based program where we r
 ead stories and make them come alive with our bodies!\nJoin Megan Snider\,
  author and Founder of Appleseed Yoga for Kids as she delivers inspiring s
 tories and gets the whole family moving.\nClass begins and ends with song 
 and breathwork and is filled with pages of creativity and activity. Kids a
 nd families can sit quietly and listen\, do partial poses or make up their
  own\, following our lead.\nIt's ALL yoga! No experience\, mats\, or mater
 ials required.\nFor children ages 0-5.\nRegistration required.\nInformatio
 n Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected b
 y the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(
 a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pr
 ogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libr
 ary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswe
 rline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room\, Ground Floor
